airunner for Debian
------------------

This is the SERVICES-ONLY apt packaging of AIRunner (issue #2237). It
contains no Qt desktop client by owner decision. Supported on
Ubuntu 26.04 and newer (the sqlalchemy 2.x dependency is not
available on 24.04; issue #2250). What you get:

  * Python package airunner-services built from services/ via pybuild,
    exposing the airunner-daemon, airunner-headless and
    airunner-service console scripts in /usr/bin (plus the download
    and migration helpers from SERVICE_CONSOLE_SCRIPTS).
  * systemd unit airunner-headless.service, enabled on install,
    running loopback-only by default (daemon 127.0.0.1:8188,
    HTTP 127.0.0.1:8080).
  * Default config seeded to /etc/airunner/daemon.yaml on first
    install; writable state in /var/lib/airunner, logs journaled
    (file logging only when the daemon config enables it).

airunner-common 6.1.7 is vendored as files (debian/vendor/README.source,
issue #2243): dh_python3 cannot map it to a distro package yet, and the
daemon cannot boot without it. This becomes a real Depends once
airunner-common publishes its own Debian binary.

Heavy ML extras (torch/cu129 wheels, diffusers, llama-cpp-python and
friends) are not Debian-packaged. Without torch the daemon boots in
degraded mode: /health stays reachable, sidecar-backed modalities
(Ollama/llama.cpp) keep working, and local generation endpoints report
missing-runtime diagnostics (502/503) instead of tracebacks. Install
extras from PyPI into a venv when a workload needs local models:

    /usr/bin/python3 -m venv /opt/airunner-ml && \
    /opt/airunner-ml/bin/pip install 'airunner-services[headless]'

Config: edit /etc/airunner/daemon.yaml, then
`systemctl restart airunner-headless`. Logs: `journalctl -u
airunner-headless`.

